"q-131171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-131171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x"] ["math" "\\frac{1+xy}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{xy}"] ["math" "x(y+1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,i+(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,j+(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,k.$ \nFind $∇\\cdot F.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((2x+3y-4z)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}((2x+3y-4z)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((2x+3y-4z)^{2}) \\\\  & =4(2x+3y-4z)+6(2x+3y-4z)-8(2x+3y-4z) \\\\  & =2(2x+3y-4z) \\\\  & =4x+6y-8z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2x+3y-4z)^{2}"] ["math" "4x+6y-8z"] ["math" "6x+9y-12z"] ["math" "8x+12y-16z"] ["math" "x+2y-4z"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x+6y-8z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=⟨{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz,\\,xyz,2⟩.$ Find $\\text{div}\\,F.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz+xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡yz"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡yz+xz"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡yz+xz+2"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz+xyz+2"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz+xz"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-123176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡yz+xz"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=x(y{e}^{z}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,i+xy{e}^{z}\\,j+z(x+1)\\,k.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(1,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x(y{e}^{z}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z(x+1)) \\\\  & =(y{e}^{z}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+x{e}^{z}+(x+1) \\\\  & =y{e}^{z}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x{e}^{z}+x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(1,1,0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(1,1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1\\cdot {e}^{0}+1+1 \\\\  & =1+0+1+1+1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=2xy{z}^{2}\\,i+x{e}^{y}\\,j+y{z}^{3}\\,k.$ \nFind $∇\\cdot F.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =2y{z}^{2}+x{e}^{y}+3y{z}^{2} \\\\  & =5y{z}^{2}+x{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5y{z}^{2}+x{e}^{y}"] ["math" "x+{e}^{y}+{z}^{2}"] ["math" "xy{z}^{2}+xz"] ["math" "y{z}^{2}+xy+y"] ["math" "y{z}^{2}+xy{e}^{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5y{z}^{2}+x{e}^{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+y{x}^{2}\\,j+x{z}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,k.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(1,0,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}+2xz{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(1,0,-2),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(1,0,-2) & =(-2)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0+{1}^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =-2+1-4 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-131178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-105578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/33f0353e3856fb2b458d17ed1959918e6a3dd96fd0a966d971575ffc212402f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-105578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move horizontally and vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-105578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609dfb73f0162bc2599f430419dca3ba7eb7de4cd61195c39c1bb543815bd"} {"question" "q-105578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-105578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/state.json" "file_sha256" "063b2c62c2e929429d2be6666f0a83af25ad862030455b110c8d7becbbd11a3c"} {"question" "q-10